{
  "acceptance": null,
  "change": {
    "task": "Hotfix: install-step stalls in the Casper profile workflows and the TLA+ invariant check",
    "base": "679e2b4c1b929184a4f67d3f9c879d23599d6f29",
    "origin": "On 2026-10-23 the Ubuntu package mirror of the hosted runners was very slow. In PR #826 and PR #827, apt-get install default-jre took 12.5 to 15 minutes, and the 15-minute job timeout stopped the TLA+ invariant check and two profile checks before verification ran.",
    "change": "Each of the nine install steps uses the JDK 21 of the runner image (JAVA_HOME_21_X64) instead of apt-get update and apt-get install default-jre. The step puts that JDK first on PATH for the later steps and prints its version. jq and wget come from the runner image, and command -v checks them. Each install step has timeout-minutes: 5, so a slow step fails with its own name.",
    "java": "default-jre on Ubuntu noble installs OpenJDK 21. The runner image provides Temurin JDK 21, so the Java major version for TLC does not change.",
    "unchanged": "The TLA+ tools version (v1.7.4), its download, its sha256 check, the models, the fixtures, the verification commands, the job timeouts, and the triggers are unchanged."
  },
  "expected_failure": "Six workflows belong to discharged claims (CLAIM-CASPER-SOAK-003 to 008). Until the maintainer accepts this change and the ledgers are rebound, check-casper-claims fails with 'The discharged source or specification differs.' in the Slashing test suite. The ledgers are not rebound before the acceptance.",
